<nav>
  <a class="logo" href="/"><svg class="logomark" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="1.4" y="2.9" width="17.2" height="12.4" rx="2.1" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/><path d="M4.3 6.7l2.6 2.3-2.6 2.3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><rect x="8.3" y="10.3" width="3.3" height="1.5" rx="0.3" fill="var(--pine)"/><path d="M6.5 17.4h7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>ditty</a>
  <span class="grow"></span>
  <a href="#recipes" class="hidem">Recipes</a>
  <a href="#install">Install</a>
  <a href="/quickstart/">Docs</a>
  <a href="https://github.com/0funct0ry/ditty" class="gh">GitHub</a>
</nav>

<header class="hero">
  <div class="staffbg" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Share a terminal over the web.</h1>
    <p class="lede">One command turns any shell, log tail or TUI into a link you can send. Read-only by default, so watching is safe and typing is a decision.</p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn" href="#install">Install ditty</a>
      <a class="btn alt" href="#recipes">See the recipes</a>
      <span class="instant">
        <span class="pill"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="4" y="2" width="16" height="20" rx="2"/><path d="M9 22v-4h6v4"/></svg>one binary</span>
        <span class="pill"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/></svg>zero config</span>
        <span class="pill"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2 4 5v6c0 5 3.5 8.5 8 11 4.5-2.5 8-6 8-11V5z"/></svg>secure by default</span>
      </span>
    </div>

    <div class="demo">
      <figure class="shot">
        <figcaption>Run this</figcaption>
        <img src="/assets/ditty-top.gif" alt="Terminal showing ditty top being invoked, printing the startup banner with the session URL." loading="lazy">
      </figure>
      <figure class="shot">
        <figcaption>They see this</figcaption>
        <img src="/assets/ditty-top-web.gif" alt="The same ditty top session, live and read-only, open in a web browser." loading="lazy">
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-note">Whoever opens the link watches live. Neither installed anything, and neither could type.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section id="install">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="install">
      <h2>Install</h2>
      <div class="cols">
        <div>
          <h4>Homebrew</h4>
          <div class="cmd">
            <pre>brew install 0funct0ry/tap/ditty</pre>
            <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy command">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/></svg>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4>Go</h4>
          <div class="cmd">
            <pre>go install github.com/0funct0ry/ditty@latest</pre>
            <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy command">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/></svg>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4>Docker</h4>
          <div class="cmd">
            <pre>docker run -p 7654:7654 ghcr.io/0funct0ry/ditty htop</pre>
            <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy command">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/></svg>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4>Install script</h4>
          <div class="cmd">
            <pre>curl -fsSL https://github.com/0funct0ry/ditty/releases/latest/download/install.sh | sh</pre>
            <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy command">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/></svg>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tight">
  <div class="wrap invariants">
    <div class="inv">
      <h3><span>invariant one</span>Nobody types unless you say so</h3>
      <div>
        <p>Input from a browser is discarded on the server, before it reaches the pseudo-terminal. The browser has no switch to flip. Pass <code>-w</code> and you have opted in, deliberately, in the command you typed.</p>
        <pre><span class="d">$</span> ditty htop              <span class="d"># watchers only</span>
<span class="d">$</span> ditty -w tmux attach     <span class="d"># now they can drive</span></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="inv">
      <h3><span>invariant two</span>It refuses to expose a shell by accident</h3>
      <div>
        <p>Binding anywhere other than localhost without an authentication method doesn't warn you. It stops, and tells you exactly which flag to add.</p>
        <pre><span class="d">$</span> ditty -a 0.0.0.0 bash
<span class="r">ditty: refusing to listen on 0.0.0.0:7654 without authentication.</span>

  This would expose `bash` to your entire network.

  Pick one:
    <span class="g">--token</span>                  random URL token
    <span class="g">--basic-auth</span> user:pass   HTTP basic authentication
    <span class="g">--client-ca</span> ca.pem       mutual TLS
    <span class="y">--insecure-no-auth</span>       I understand; do it anyway</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="inv">
      <h3><span>invariant three</span>The URL is a secret by default</h3>
      <div>
        <p>Every session gets a random token, even on localhost. It lives in the path and is swapped for a cookie on first load, so it never reaches proxy logs or a <code>Referer</code> header. The full link is printed at startup, so zero-config stays zero-config.</p>
        <pre><span class="d">$</span> ditty --open vim notes.md
  url       <span class="g">http://127.0.0.1:7654/t/2b81f0ac94d7e365</span>
  <span class="d">opening your browser…</span></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="recipes">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Some ways people actually use ditty</h2>
    <p class="sub">ditty bridges one pseudo-terminal to browsers and gets out of the way — everything else here composes it with tools you already run, like tmux, Docker and nginx. See the <a href="/recipes/shared-session/">full recipe pages</a> for the risks and failure modes of each.</p>
    <div class="recipes">
      <div class="recipe">
        <span class="num">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Let two people drive one shell</h3>
          <p>tmux already handles multiple typists and survives ditty restarting. Use it.</p>
          <pre>tmux new -s work
ditty -w tmux attach -t work</pre>
          <a class="more" href="/recipes/shared-session/">Read the full recipe <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="recipe">
        <span class="num">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Broadcast a log or a dashboard</h3>
          <p>Colours, cursor moves and full-screen redraws all survive the trip. Joining mid-flight repaints instantly.</p>
          <pre>ditty htop
ditty tail -f /var/log/nginx/access.log</pre>
          <a class="more" href="/recipes/read-only-broadcast/">Read the full recipe <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="recipe">
        <span class="num">03</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Hand a shell to someone you don't trust</h3>
          <p>ditty is not a sandbox and never claims to be. Make the container the sandbox.</p>
          <pre>ditty -w docker run --rm -it --network none --memory 256m alpine sh</pre>
          <a class="more" href="/recipes/sandboxed-shell/">Read the full recipe <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="recipe">
        <span class="num">04</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Put it behind your existing SSO</h3>
          <p>Serve on a Unix socket, let nginx or oauth2-proxy decide who gets in, and trust the header it sets.</p>
          <pre>ditty --socket /run/ditty.sock --base-path /term \
  --trust-proxy 127.0.0.1/32 \
  --trust-header X-Auth-Request-Email bash</pre>
          <a class="more" href="/recipes/behind-nginx-sso/">Read the full recipe <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="recipe">
        <span class="num">05</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Send a link that self-destructs</h3>
          <p>One client, ever. Thirty seconds after they close the tab, the process is gone.</p>
          <pre>ditty --once --wait-for-client 5m --detach-grace 30s -w bash</pre>
          <a class="more" href="/recipes/one-shot-support-link/">Read the full recipe <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="recipe">
        <span class="num">06</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Debug a container from a browser</h3>
          <p>Distroless image, no shell inside it, your command supplies the shell.</p>
          <pre>docker run -p 7654:7654 -e DITTY_BASIC_AUTH=me:hunter2 \
  ghcr.io/0funct0ry/ditty -w sh</pre>
          <a class="more" href="/docker/">Read about the container images <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tight">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Reconnecting doesn't lose the screen</h2>
    <p class="sub">ditty keeps the last 256 KB of terminal output in a ring buffer. Every client that attaches — first join or after your laptop slept through a tunnel — gets that replayed before live output resumes. You come back to <code>htop</code>, not to a blank rectangle.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tight">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Things ditty will not do</h2>
    <p class="sub">Stated up front, so you don't discover them later. See <a href="/security/">Security</a> for the full picture.</p>
    <div class="honest">
      <div><h4>It is not a sandbox</h4><p>A read-only session still exposes whatever the program can do. <code>--writable</code> on <code>less</code> or <code>vim</code> is a shell. Use a container when the audience is untrusted.</p></div>
      <div><h4>It has no user accounts</h4><p>There is optional SQLite login for small teams. For anything real, put ditty behind the identity provider you already run.</p></div>
      <div><h4>It does not multiplex</h4><p>tmux and screen are excellent at persistence and multiple typists. ditty attaches to them rather than competing with them.</p></div>
      <div><h4>It does not emulate a shell</h4><p>Every session is a real pseudo-terminal running a real process. If it doesn't work in your terminal, it won't work here either.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

